WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.100
Why a runbook?

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.488
Because each second lab
proved one piece on its own.

3
00:00:04.488 --> 00:00:08.950
A deployment proves them together,
against an environment someone depends on.

4
00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:13.711
Stage 1 is a live test: an Entra test
tenant, an Azure test subscription

5
00:00:13.711 --> 00:00:18.138
and an Active Directory test
forest, with production's licenses.

6
00:00:18.138 --> 00:00:22.960
Stage 2 is production, a separate tenant,
so nothing the test stage does can

7
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.625
reach it, and its preflight won't start
unless the test smoke test passed.

8
00:00:27.625 --> 00:00:31.920
The commands are the same both times;
only the settings file changes.
